## 4. Touch-Friendly UI Design

### Touch Target Sizing (2026 Standards)

**Minimum touch target size: 44x44px** (Apple HIG, Material Design, WCAG)

```css
/* Ensure all interactive elements are touch-friendly */
button,
a,
input,
select {
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  padding: 12px 16px;
}

/* On touch devices, increase to 48px */
@media (hover: none) and (pointer: coarse) {
  button,
  a,
  input,
  select {
    min-height: 48px;
    min-width: 48px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
  }
}
```

### Touch Gesture Support

```css
/* Enable smooth scrolling on mobile */
html {
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}

/* Prevent text selection on double-tap */
.no-select {
  -webkit-user-select: none;
  user-select: none;
  -webkit-touch-callout: none;
}

/* Prevent iOS zoom on input focus */
input, select, textarea {
  font-size: 16px; /* iOS won't zoom if >= 16px */
}
```

### Touch Feedback

```css
/* Provide instant visual feedback */
button {
  transition: transform 0.1s ease, background 0.2s ease;
}

button:active {
  transform: scale(0.98);
  background: rgba(136, 192, 208, 0.2);
}

/* Remove hover effects on touch devices */
@media (hover: none) {
  button:hover {
    transform: none;
  }
}
```

### Spacing for Touch

- **Minimum spacing between targets**: 8px
- **Recommended spacing**: 16px
- **Thumb zone**: Bottom 1/3 of screen most accessible
- **One-handed use**: Place primary actions within thumb reach

