## 5. CSS Grid + Flexbox (The Dynamic Duo)

### When to Use Each

**Flexbox** excels at **one-dimensional layouts**:
- Navigation bars
- Card content alignment
- Centering elements
- Distributing space along one axis

**CSS Grid** excels at **two-dimensional layouts**:
- Page layouts
- Card grids
- Dashboard layouts
- Complex responsive patterns

### Modern Grid Patterns

```css
/* Auto-fit responsive grid (no media queries!) */
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
  gap: 2rem;
}

/* Named grid areas for semantic layouts */
.layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header"
    "sidebar main"
    "footer footer";
  grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr;
  gap: 1rem;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .layout {
    grid-template-areas:
      "header"
      "main"
      "sidebar"
      "footer";
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
```

### Flexbox Modern Patterns

```css
/* Responsive flex with wrapping */
.flex-container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.flex-item {
  flex: 1 1 300px; /* Grow, shrink, base 300px */
}

/* Space between with gap (no margin hacks!) */
.navbar {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1rem;
```

