## VEA-R2: instance-bound spatial relation probe

Hypothesis `REL-REGION-01`:

> Subject/object region features plus explicit pair geometry improve exact-negative recall over a global image relation head.

Start with the same four OpenImages relation tasks to isolate architecture. Each record must bind:

- subject and object class/MID;
- subject and object box;
- decoded RGB hash;
- subject-region tokens;
- object-region tokens;
- normalized box geometry and overlap;
- upstream opportunity IDs.

Arms:

1. frozen global AAP64 head baseline;
2. subject/object region features;
3. region features plus box geometry.

Required controls:

- subject/object box swap;
- wrong object box in the same image;
- wrong image;
- zero regions.

Pilot gate on one seed:

- macro BA at least `0.68`;
- exact-negative recall at least `0.65`;
- lower CI for region+geometry minus global BA above zero;
- subject/object swap changes directional predicates in the expected direction;
- 100% entity/box/evidence provenance.

Only a passing pilot expands to three seeds and additional predicates `{left_of,right_of,above,below,inside,contains}`. New predicates require their own minimum-cell audit and inverse/symmetry tests.

Estimated pilot: 1–2 GPU hours after corpus materialization.

## VEA-G1: deterministic scene-graph assembler

Hypothesis `GRAPH-COMP-01`:

> Accepted atomic modules can be composed into a more reliable scene graph without another learned model.

CPU-only first implementation. Nodes and edges are admitted only with evidence IDs and module/checkpoint hashes.

Required invariants:

- canonical entity identity and aliases;
- inverse edges (`left_of/right_of`, `inside/contains`, `above/below`);
- symmetric edges where applicable;
- no self-relations unless the predicate explicitly permits them;
- explicit conflict/unresolved states;
- no unsupported edge generation;
- per-node/edge confidence and provenance.

Metrics on sealed public-GT scenes:

- node precision/recall/F1;
- edge precision/recall/F1;
- inverse consistency;
- contradiction rate;
- unsupported-edge rate;
- evidence coverage.

Gate: unsupported-edge rate `0`, inverse consistency at least `0.99`, contradiction rate below `0.01`, and graph edge F1 no worse than the contributing relation module after entity matching.

## VEA-C1: small-VLM typed scene consumer

This experiment remains blocked until presence, at least one property family, relations, and graph composition have passed their own holdouts.

Hypothesis `SCENE-CONSUME-01`:

> A native small VLM can use a provenance-bound typed scene graph without degrading its native visual reasoning.

Target backbone: the current supported Qwen3-VL/Qwen3.5 4B-class path, not Muse.

Identical sealed episodes:

- native RGB only;
- native RGB plus real graph;
- native RGB plus empty graph;
- native RGB plus shuffled graph;
- native RGB plus wrong-scene graph.

Outputs are structured fact bundle plus short scene description. Promotion requires 100% provenance, helpful flips greater than harmful flips, real graph better than zero/shuffle/wrong with positive paired intervals, and no material loss of native-only object recall.

Estimated budget: 2–6 GPU hours after prerequisites. No earlier LoRA run is authorized.

